{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The reroute is traffic-justified under POL-RD-23. EV-ADVIS-05008-01 is an LTA TRAFFIC_ADVISORY of type HEAVY_TRAFFIC - a type the policy's traffic_justification_types maps onto 'congestion' - for the Kallang-Paya Lebar Expressway (KPE) towards TPE after Sims Way exit, valid 19:09:23 to 20:19:23, and it therefore overlaps the trip window 19:29:23 to 19:52:23 (overlaps_trip_window true). The recommended route recorded in EV-TRIP-05008 runs via the KPE, and the trip record's own route_deviation_detected event places the exit at 'KPE / Sims Way exit' - the same road and the same location the advisory names. The advisory's derived block leaves intersects_route undetermined for the Judge rather than deciding it, but the record's own road and location labels put the congestion on the very segment the driver was driving at the time, so POL-RD-23's condition is satisfied and this was not a discretionary detour.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05008-01", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.road/location against trip_record.optimal_route_via and trip_record.events[route_deviation_detected]",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver gave the notice POL-RD-21 requires, and gave it before the point of deviation. MSG-05008-003 was sent at 19:34:22, delivered at 19:34:23 and read at 19:35:00, and it states both the reason and the intended alternative: 'Miss, KPE very jam after Sims Way, I come out at Sims Ave and go Aljunied ok? Faster.' That is the brief reason POL-RD-21 asks for, and it is in-app chat, which POL-RD-21 accepts without any call recording. The trace's first off-route fix is the Sims Avenue fix at 19:36:53 and the trip record's deviation event is at 19:37:02, so the notice preceded the deviation by over two minutes. POL-RD-21 obliges the driver to inform the rider of a traffic reroute; it does not oblige him to obtain consent, and consent is a separate element that only row (a) of POL-RD-24 turns on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008", "EV-GPS-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[MSG-05008-003] against trip_record.events[route_deviation_detected].at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is 1.50 km and is over tolerance. EV-TRIP-05008 records actual_distance_km 11.4 and optimal_distance_km 9.9, and POL-RD-22 makes the deviation their difference - 1.50 km - measured from the platform's recorded distances, not from the trace, because a sparse trace understates a route's length (the trace's own 9.584 km would understate it here). The 1.0 km tolerance in POL-RD-22 is therefore exceeded, and the 2.0 km AI limb in POL-RD-25 is expressly not applied (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied false, EV-TRIP-05008 derived), so nothing on the distance side of the policy closes this case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05008", "EV-GPS-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.deviation.deviation_km (1.50) vs tolerance_km (1.0)",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither refund row of POL-RD-24 is met, so the 1.08 SGD has no row to stand on. Row (b) refunds the excess distance fare where the reroute is traffic-justified but the rider was not informed - the rider was informed by in-app chat before the deviation (MSG-05008-003 at 19:34:22, read 19:35:00), so (b) fails. Row (d) refunds where the reroute is not traffic-justified - the LTA HEAVY_TRAFFIC advisory on the KPE at the trip time justifies it, so (d) fails. The 1.08 SGD in EV-FARE-05008 is exactly the excess distance fare (deviation_km 1.50 x per_km_rate_sgd 0.72, no surge applied), and the matrix pays that figure only in rows (b) and (d). The interim recovery of it from the driver's earnings should not be finalised on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05008", "EV-CHAT-05008", "EV-ADVIS-05008-01", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd against POL-RD-24 rows (b) and (d)",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The case fits no row of POL-RD-24, and the clause itself says what happens then: 'A case that fits no row (for example, informed but the rider objected) is escalated under POL-GEN-26.' That is this case precisely - traffic-justified, the driver informed the rider before the point of deviation, and the rider answering in MSG-05008-004 'No need, pls just stay on KPE, I don't mind the jam' and in MSG-05008-005 'Eh I said no need already, why still exit'. Row (a)'s 'informed and agreed' is therefore not made out, and rows (c) and (e) cannot apply to a 1.50 km deviation. The escalation is directed by the matrix on its own terms, not manufactured out of any gap in the record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008", "EV-ADVIS-05008-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[MSG-05008-004, MSG-05008-005] against POL-RD-24 row (a)",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the fare state in EV-FARE-05008 - payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 1.08, recovered from the driver's earnings pending review - the values POL-RD-24 licenses do not treat the driver alike, and POL-GEN-03 fixes their meaning. NO_ACTION is party-relative and leaves the present state standing, which here is the very refund the driver contests; PARTIAL_REFUND returns part of the trip's charge to the rider and would confirm the same 1.08 against him. ESCALATE issues no monetary outcome and holds the amount for the human reviewer, and it is the only licensed disposition that does not close the money against the driver while the 'informed but the rider objected' question is unresolved.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status and fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither side's snapshot carries a fraud flag - EV-DPROF-05008 records driver_profile.fraud_flags 0 and EV-RPROF-05008 carries no fraud flag field - so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 uplift is not engaged and the confidence this case is held to is not raised against the driver. Beyond that single field, POL-GEN-01 makes every other field on either profile context only: it may inform how closely a party's assertions are scrutinised, but it may never establish a fact about this trip or decide it. The rider's history cannot substitute for the chat log, the advisory or the recorded distances on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-05008", "EV-RPROF-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-GEN-22"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.fraud_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The record is complete on every artifact this claim set relies on: EV-TRIP-05008, EV-GPS-05008, EV-CHAT-05008, EV-FARE-05008, EV-RPROF-05008, EV-DPROF-05008 and EV-ADVIS-05008-01 each carry status COMPLETE and weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes fired. POL-GEN-02's discount rule therefore depresses nothing, the GPS trace at 47 fixes and 100 per cent coverage needs no disclosure caveat, and the escalation sought here is the escalation POL-RD-24 directs for a case that fits no row - not an escalation for a fact the record cannot establish.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05008", "EV-TRIP-05008"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[].admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the substance, and the record bears it out: the recommended route was 9.9 km and the route actually driven was 11.4 km (EV-TRIP-05008), a deviation of 1.50 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance in POL-RD-22. The excess distance fare is 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.08 SGD, with no surge (POL-RD-24, EV-FARE-05008) — the same 1.08 SGD already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver. The 2.0 km AI ceiling in POL-RD-25 is not applied (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false), and in any event 1.50 km is under it.\n\nOn traffic (POL-RD-23): the LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05008-01 records HEAVY_TRAFFIC on the KPE towards TPE after the Sims Way exit, valid 19:09-20:19, overlapping the 19:29-19:52 trip window. The advisory's derived block leaves 'intersects route' undetermined and leaves that call to me; reading its road, direction and location against the trip, the recommended route runs via the KPE and the trip's own deviation event puts the exit at the KPE / Sims Way exit, so the congestion sat on the segment the driver was on. I find the reroute traffic-justified. So the driver's claim that justification is made out is accepted, and the rider's alternative argument that this is the unjustified branch (row (d)) is rejected: the advisory carries the justification.\n\nOn notice (POL-RD-21): the driver did what the clause asks — MSG-05008-003 at 19:34:22 gave the reason and the intended alternative in-app, ahead of the deviation detected at 19:37:02 — so his notice claim is accepted. But POL-RD-21 makes a deviation 'agreed' only where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment, and the platform's own log records the opposite: MSG-05008-004 at 19:34:52 ('No need, pls just stay on KPE, I don't mind the jam') and MSG-05008-005 at 19:38:22 ('Eh I said no need already, why still exit'). The rider did not agree, and the rider's claim on this point is accepted.\n\nThat places this case squarely in POL-RD-24's own words: 'informed but the rider objected.' No lettered row fits. Row (a) requires agreement; row (b) requires that the rider was not informed (she was); rows (c) and (e) are closed by the 1.50 km deviation; row (d) requires the reroute to be unjustified (it was justified). The rider's argument that rows (b) and (d) refund the excess whatever the justification is rejected: on the facts found, neither row's conditions are met. POL-RD-24 says exactly what happens then — the case is escalated under POL-GEN-26. The driver's claim that neither refund row is met and that the matrix directs escalation is accepted; that is the outcome.\n\nThe dispute value is 1.08 SGD, below 10.00, and neither profile carries a fraud flag (driver_profile.fraud_flags 0, and the authority block records 0), so POL-GEN-22 permits a final AI ruling at any confidence and no 0.95 uplift applies. This escalation is not a deferral for want of confidence — it is the disposition the refund matrix directs on its own terms. The amount is held: no money moves now, and the 1.08 SGD already refunded is not clawed back from the driver while the human reviewer decides the 'informed but objected' question.\n\nNo referral arises. The clauses POL-GEN-03 names — POL-NS-22 (a fee other than 5.00 SGD), POL-NS-24 (goodwill credit) and POL-NS-25 (repeat no-show flag) — have nothing to apply to on a route deviation. The open question for the reviewer is the one above, and it sits here in the explanation rather than in referrals."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the driver and the rider: I am sending this trip to a human reviewer, because the route-deviation policy's refund matrix has no row for what happened here, and the matrix's own closing words send exactly this situation to a reviewer. Why the deviation is real. Under POL-RD-22 the deviation is the platform's recorded actual distance minus its recorded recommended distance: 11.40 km - 9.90 km = 1.50 km (EV-TRIP-05008). That is above the policy's 1.0 km tolerance, and POL-RD-25's 2.0 km AI ceiling is switched off, so the distance side closes nothing. Notice, but no agreement. The driver did inform the rider by in-app chat before deviating: MSG-05008-003 at 19:34:22 said the KPE was jammed after Sims Way and that he would exit to Sims Avenue / Aljunied, and the vehicle in fact left the recommended route only at 19:37:02. So the driver met POL-RD-21's duty to inform. But the rider did not agree - MSG-05008-004 at 19:34:52 said 'No need, pls just stay on KPE, I don't mind the jam', and MSG-05008-005 at 19:38:22 repeated the objection. Row (a) of POL-RD-24 needs the rider informed AND agreed, and the agreement limb fails on the platform's own log. The matrix. POL-RD-24 refunds the excess distance fare (1.50 km x 0.72/km = 1.08 SGD) in row (b), which needs the rider not to have been informed - she was informed, so (b) does not apply - and in row (d), which needs the reroute not to be traffic-justified. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05008-01 (HEAVY_TRAFFIC on the KPE towards TPE after the Sims Way exit, valid 19:09-20:19) covers the recommended route segment at the trip time, so the reroute was traffic-justified under POL-RD-23 and (d) does not apply either. Rows (c) and (e) need a deviation of 1 km or less. So no row applies. POL-RD-24 says in terms that a case fitting no row - 'informed but the rider objected' - is escalated under POL-GEN-26, and that is this case. What this means for the 1.08 SGD. The interim refund shown in EV-FARE-05008 (refund_issued_sgd 1.08, payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED) is neither confirmed nor reversed here: on an escalation no monetary outcome issues and the amount is held for the reviewer. The drivers' argument that no refund row is met and the rider's argument that (b) and (d) each return the excess fare both fail on the same facts - (b) is unavailable because the rider was informed, (d) because the reroute was justified - and the policy's answer to the remaining configuration is escalation, not either party's preferred outcome. No referral is added: the referral clauses POL-GEN-03 names (POL-NS-24, POL-NS-25, POL-NS-22) concern no-show cases and are not engaged. Neither party's profile carries a fraud flag (EV-DPROF-05008 driver_profile.fraud_flags 0; EV-RPROF-05008 none), so POL-GEN-22's 0.95 uplift is not triggered, and every other profile field is context only under POL-GEN-01. Every artifact used is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped below the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires; this escalation rests on the matrix, not on low confidence. The open question for the reviewer is whether a driver who gave the notice POL-RD-21 requires, but proceeded over the rider's express objection, should keep the 1.08 SGD excess distance fare."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
